WEBVTT

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:20.320
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:20.320
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:20.320
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:44.700
Chapter 7

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:44.700
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.540
On March 19th of Space
Year 794, Imperial Year 485...

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:57.170
...Reinhard, who had just returned from a
campaign, was delighted to receive the news...

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.410
...that he had been granted
a meeting with Annerose.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:04.700
Before the campaign, they said we were
underage and wouldn't serve us wine.

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.440
Not bad.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.360
Will you take up wine
tasting as your hobby ?

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.770
I wouldn't want to get intoxicated
to the point of stupidity.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.120
But it's a good idea to at least know how
to tell the difference between wines.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.650
Not having a hobby isn't
particularly commendable, either.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:32.810
It's true Lord Reinhard has a tendency
to be disinterested and thrifty.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:39.110
Plus, we'll probably have lots of
spare time until the next campaign.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:44.650
I'm sure you could think of other ways to
kill time that other people couldn't dream of.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.330
Such as ?

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.000
Finding love.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.050
I can try, but how do
I find my counterpart ?

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.910
Lord Reinhard, to decide to love
and then find someone to love...

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.590
...it's not usually the
order in which love happens.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:12.440
The "order" depends on
the individual, doesn't it ?

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.180
In general,
I suppose so, but...

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:19.970
If I have the intention to pursue it and
if I'm prepared for the occurrence...

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:23.220
...then I should be able to find someone
who matches up well with me.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.930
Don't you agree, Kircheis ?

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.620
Then I'd like to ask you:
what kind of woman do you like ?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.100
I'd like to know
for future reference.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.900
I don't have a
particular type in mind.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:41.440
Let's see, if she's intelligent and
kindhearted, that's more than enough.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.920
In other words, you're not serious
about pursuing love right now, correct ?

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.150
Come to think of it, people are
praising you for your continence.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:01.240
It's annoying to receive
strange praise from monkeys.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:07.320
If they don't have the brain to understand
my virtue, how can they praise me ?

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:12.380
But at least it's better than those people who speak ill of you without understanding you, isn't it ?

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.570
As I said before...

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:22.350
...you're the type who finds something
virtuous even in the bottom of a sewer.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.870
If you were
a school teacher...

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:28.130
...there would be no student in that
school whose feelings would get hurt.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:33.500
What's with you ?

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.260
You look strange.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:40.200
Ah, no, it's just that my parents
used to say something similar.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.820
Come to think of it,
how are your parents ?

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.570
They're well.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.940
You haven't seen them
for a long time, have you ?

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.590
Why don't you
return home sometime ?

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.070
Thank you.

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.760
Then I'll do so
when I get a chance.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:04:59.900
Yeah.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.130
Will you come with me ?

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.080
No, I won't go.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.520
I'm different from you.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:22.770
There's no one in
that house anymore.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.320
Lord Reinhard...

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:48.970
On May 20th, Herman von
Luneberg, along with his wife...

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:53.770
...paid a visit to High Admiral Ovlessor, Chief
Commander of Armored Ground Warfare.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:59.280
The official purpose of the visit was to pay his
respects when promoted to Rear Admiral...

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.400
...but there was much more
to what he was thinking about.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:16.720
That Musel brat also
became a Rear Admiral.

00:06:17.870 --> 00:06:24.680
What do time-oblivious, conservative
people like Ovlessor think about it ?

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:27.970
Right now, he's
just a Rear Admiral...

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:31.080
...but if he gets promoted to Vice
Admiral, then to Admiral and higher...

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:38.470
...those aristocrats with their proud lineages will have to defer to him in accordance with custom.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.270
Darling...

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.100
Be quiet.{Shut up.}

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:55.000
If those aristocrats think that they need
my power to prevent such a predicament...

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:01.550
...then I can promote myself to
them or have them indebted to me.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:19.680
Elizabeth.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.450
Hey, Elizabeth !

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:24.630
I'm sorry, but I'm feeling...

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:49.570
I'm sorry to make you witness a
scene like that, My Lord High Admiral.{General.}

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:55.400
Your wife doesn't
seem to like my house.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:01.560
I suppose you forced
her to come along ?

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.130
N...no, no such thing.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:06.950
Anyway.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:08.220
Take a seat.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:08.740
Yes, sir.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:09.920
If you'll excuse me.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.950
He's completely seized the
leadership of this table.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:18.250
This is all because Elizabeth
fell ill at the worst time.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:19.770
Dammit.

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:25.140
Now, what brings
you here today ?

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:30.720
Since I was appointed to be a Rear Admiral
recently, I wanted to pay my respects to you...

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.220
...as you are the chief
commander of ground warfare.

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:37.750
I hate roundabout tactics !

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:42.850
You didn't come here
just for that, did you ?

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.790
If you have things to say,
say them straight out !

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.770
Now, what did you
really come here for ?

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:59.350
To tell you the truth, it's about
Rear Admiral Reinhard von Musel, but...

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.210
Ha, the blond brat.

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:10.750
His sister's sex appeal
bewitched{crazed} the Kaiser.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:15.130
It has trickled down to him -
that's all there is to it.

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:19.310
It bothers you,
Rear Admiral Luneberg ?

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:26.180
But he himself has so much confidence
in his military talent, and to be fair...

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:31.970
...that assessment is not
entirely delusional on his part.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.670
As I thought,
he's interested.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.970
Looks like you don't have much to do
since returning from the battlefield...

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.370
...Rear Admiral Luneberg.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.000
Huh ?

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:51.300
You take the trouble to come to a person's
house and gossip about that brat ?

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.150
You're an expert
in ground warfare.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:02.250
The reverse of it is that you can't
expect to be promoted to Fleet Admiral.

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:06.770
You are aiming for my
position, aren't you ?

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.150
That's what I would think.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:11.150
That...

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.560
I hate that blond brat, but...

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:20.350
I hate you, too.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:26.220
So I'll be straight with you,
Rear Admiral Luneburg.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:35.870
I'll be happy if you and that blond brat battle
it out with each other and you both fall.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:43.320
You should just hone your fangs
to rip out his pale thin neck.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.110
My plan has failed.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:04.600
Ovlessor is simple, but
he's not easy to manipulate.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:14.300
If you win over him, you'll
have opportunities for the future.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:24.760
But it's only in your dreams that
we'd cooperate with your efforts...

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.220
...to bring down
the blond brat.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:44.770
Kircheis, it's strange
to ask you this again...

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:47.790
...but what do you
think of Luneberg ?

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:52.970
It'll be troublesome if he
becomes our enemy, but...

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.550
If he becomes our ally, that
would be even more troublesome.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:07.240
Kircheis, you are harsher
than I thought you were.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:12.540
If you spend eight years with Lord
Reinhard, you can't help but be like that.

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:16.300
Then am I some
sort of a virus ?

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.930
We can't trust Luneberg...

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.920
There is that...

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:32.630
But also, since you have no desire
to serve under other people...

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:38.200
...you can't establish relationships with others unless you make them recognize your ascendancy.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:44.640
Judging from what we know so far, it's
impossible to expect that from Luneburg.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.470
You're certainly right.

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:57.210
You might not be interested
in matters like this, but...

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.620
Kircheis related to Reinhard...

00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:06.500
...several pieces of information he
had gathered regarding Luneberg.

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:13.420
They included the fact that the relationship
between Luneberg and his wife...

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:15.970
...is far from being
characterized as a honeymoon.

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:24.000
That Elizabeth married Luneberg
against her wishes after her fiancé died...

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.340
...was related to Reinhard
for the first time.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:40.340
So Lady Luneberg married
a man she didn't love ?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.910
In summary, that's
probably how it is.

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.770
But to be honest, it's
no more than a rumor.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:51.490
Then I feel sorry for the man who
became a husband in such circumstances.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:57.610
If you're not in love,
you shouldn't marry.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.080
Unless you are forced to...

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:21.920
Lord Reinhard...

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:29.670
It seems that Luneberg isn't a
particularly happy man, after all.

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:41.570
But even if Luneberg finds out that
Lord Reinhard sympathizes with him...

00:14:41.570 --> 00:14:44.280
...I don't think he would be pleased
or think he's gained a friend.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:49.900
And that must be the biggest reason why
these two people will never become allies.

00:14:57.010 --> 00:15:03.770
On May 24th, Reinhard and Kircheis
were granted a meeting with Annerose...

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:09.970
...at the residence of Viscountess Schafhausen,
one of the few friends Annerose has at court.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.440
It is not easy for
the two to meet Annerose.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:21.970
When they return from campaigns, they are
permitted a meeting as a sort of reward...

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:23.770
...for their achievements
on the battlefield.

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:37.830
In this meeting Reinhard told Annerose of the circumstances where Kircheis wasn't promoted.

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:43.300
I understand.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:46.300
I'll ask the Kaiser to
do something about it.

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:55.240
Thank you, Lady Annerose.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:59.930
But I don't need to be
hasty about my promotion.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.940
As it is, my promotion
rate has been fairly quick.

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:08.140
I can't let Lady Annerose
risk her position for my sake.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.830
Sieg, you are...

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.990
Lady Annerose understands.

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:26.850
In the end, Annerose understood how
Kircheis felt, and didn't interfere in the affair.

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:34.440
But despite that, a week later, Kircheis
was promoted to Lieutenant Commander.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:47.870
Reinhard was delighted,
and also surprised...

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:52.380
...but he was more astonished to
hear who helped with the promotion.

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:59.770
The newly appointed Admiral Grimmelshausen,
had especially recommended Kircheis.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:01.970
That old man...

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:07.160
...he finally realized his end was near and must
have thought he'd do at least one good thing.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:15.320
In any case, you'll have to thank the
person who put in the recommendation.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.030
You should visit him tomorrow.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.140
I'll do that.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.700
Will you come with me ?

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:29.880
No, I want to, but I think
you should go alone this time.

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:36.870
If you can, find out what
that old man is plotting.

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:39.660
Lord Reinhard...

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.250
Thank you so much for
recommending me for this promotion.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.970
It was natural
for Commodore Musel...

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:08.150
...I mean, Rear Admiral, to be
promoted, but even I was promoted.

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:13.150
If you weren't promoted as well,
that would be unreasonable.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:17.870
You assisted Rear
Admiral Musel very well.

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:20.590
I'm flattered.

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:23.710
I don't know how to
express my gratitude.

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:31.770
But since you've been
promoted already...

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:37.520
...you shouldn't expect to be promoted
again before the end of the year.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:40.660
There's no need to worry
about such an issue.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:43.400
I think Lieutenant Commander
is more than enough for me.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.120
I sincerely thank you.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:57.000
It would have been better if Lord Reinhard
were promoted to Vice Admiral sooner.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:03.470
And also, as
belated as it is...

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:08.340
...I'd like to congratulate you on
your own promotion to Admiral.

00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:17.500
No, no, my promotion has nothing to do
with my talents or accomplishments.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.520
It's only because
I'm a viscount...

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:25.950
...and I'm the recipient of a
personal favor from the Kaiser.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:34.810
This kind of
current social custom...

00:19:34.810 --> 00:19:40.550
...Rear Admiral Musel must be
dissatisfied with it, I suppose ?

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:49.830
Rear Admiral Musel is
not at all discontented.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:55.030
He thanks the Kaiser for his good fortune in becoming a Rear Admiral while he's still in his teens.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:04.000
In your position, that's all
you can advocate, I suppose.

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:09.020
Even your consideration
and sincerity...

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:17.380
...can't mask Rear Admiral
Musel's ambition-filled eyes.

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:28.870
I have never seen such eyes
as his, so full of aspiration.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:34.230
I could never have
had such eyes myself.

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:47.830
It's unmistakeable that this old gentleman
has a high opinion of Lord Reinhard.

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:51.830
But having a high opinion of
him doesn't mean liking him.

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:56.870
Especially considering the nature of Lord
Reinhard's ambitions and aspirations...

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:11.250
But when you were 18 years old,
you must have had ambitions.

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:20.440
No, when I was 18, I had already
realized my lack of talent.

00:21:25.230 --> 00:21:31.770
What has he discerned,
or has he just fantasized ?

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:38.060
So far, I don't believe he has any
malicious intent toward Lord Reinhard.

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:41.690
But I wonder if that will be
the case in the future ?

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:44.320
As an elder...

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:52.670
...if I can offer a self-important opinion,
I will say that there's no need...

00:21:52.670 --> 00:21:58.380
...for Rear Admiral
Musel to be hasty.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.950
My Lord, to what do you
refer to as "hasty" ?

00:22:11.190 --> 00:22:15.990
About life, of course.

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:28.900
Kircheis left there as
if he were chased out.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:34.870
But it was because he had misgivings
about revealing his true feelings.

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.990
Those of a devoted retainer of an
"infidel" who plans to usurp the Empire.

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:53.320
I see, that old man
said such things.

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:59.500
I can't watch my own back.

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:03.910
But you can watch it.

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:08.010
Naturally, your sight can
sometimes be wider than mine.

00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:12.570
From your perspective, what
do you think of Grimmelshausen ?

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:19.690
Let's see, as a person, I do not
have any negative feelings.

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:26.020
Rather, I'm indebted to him,
considering the current circumstances.{apparent facts.}{of promotion}

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:32.120
But what if that old man becomes
an obstacle to us in the future ?

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:39.060
In that case, I'll
have to remove him.

00:23:43.990 --> 00:23:47.080
But is it possible
for me to do that ?

00:23:57.700 --> 00:24:01.610
On June 7th, the new personnel
assignments are officially announced.

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:05.520
Rear Admiral
Reinhard von Musel...

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:09.990
...was assigned to the General
Headquarters of the Space Fleet.

00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:13.970
This was more of a clarification of his office
rather than the assignment of a duty.

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:17.970
But Reinhard was pleased...

00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:22.290
...because it was apparent that the position
was temporary till the next campaign.

00:24:25.970 --> 00:24:30.970
Kircheis was also assigned to General
Headquarters as an Assistant to the Admiral.

00:24:30.970 --> 00:24:35.130
As ambiguous a position as it was,
he was allowed to stay close to Reinhard.

00:24:36.700 --> 00:24:41.220
The wind that day, as if to symbolize
the future path of these two men...

00:24:41.220 --> 00:24:44.000
...blew hard,
and then harder.

00:24:42.470 --> 00:24:47.020
The Hard Wind of Early Summer

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:58.080
 Even as I say it's beautiful. Even as I say it's magnificent

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:53.370
[ Aurora's Adagio ]

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:53.370
Ending Theme

00:24:49.140 --> 00:24:53.370
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:24:54.070 --> 00:24:58.330
Reinhard:

00:24:54.070 --> 00:24:58.330
Horikawa Ryo

00:24:59.320 --> 00:25:08.880
 Words fall short and I can only be amazed

00:24:59.650 --> 00:25:03.870
Luneburg:

00:24:59.650 --> 00:25:03.870
Nozawa Nachi

00:25:04.850 --> 00:25:08.940
Grimmelshausen:

00:25:04.850 --> 00:25:08.940
Saikachi Ryuuji

00:25:09.870 --> 00:25:15.380
 Darkness is a dance that flees and continues

00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:14.080
Annerose:

00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:14.080
Han Keiko

